===Etymology===
From {{der|is|non|skór}}, from {{der|is|gem-pro|*skōhaz}}, from {{der|is|ine-pro|*skewk-}}, from {{m|ine-pro|*(s)kew-||to cover}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/skouːr/|lang=is}}
*: {{rhymes|ouːr|lang=is}}

===Noun===
{{is-noun|m|skós|skór}}

# {{lb|is|footwear}} a [[shoe]]

====Derived terms====
* {{l|is|skóhorn}}
* {{l|is|vera bundinn í báða skó}} (to [[have one's hands tied]])
* {{l|is|gera skóna}} (''governs dative''; to assume something)
*: ''Það má '''gera''' því '''skóna'''.''
*:: It can be '''assumed'''.

